1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:04,029
Somewhere between the Andaman
Sea and the Gulf of Thailand,

2
00:00:04,069 --> 00:00:06,828
there's a kingdom
that nobody ever colonized.

3
00:00:07,580 --> 00:00:10,520
This is Thailand, known
as the Land of Smiles.

4
00:00:10,908 --> 00:00:12,463
Its capital is Bangkok.

5
00:00:14,853 --> 00:00:17,124
About 71 million people live here.

6
00:00:19,514 --> 00:00:23,304
It covers about 513
thousand square kilometers.

7
00:00:25,694 --> 00:00:27,312
They speak Thai and Isan.

8
00:00:27,352 --> 00:00:29,369
They say sawasdee and sabaidee.

9
00:00:31,759 --> 00:00:33,060
And they pay with the baht.

10
00:00:35,233 --> 00:00:36,353
Some fun facts.

11
00:00:38,150 --> 00:00:42,620
Thailand is the only country in Southeast
Asia that was never colonized.

12
00:00:42,660 --> 00:00:47,380
Britain and France each wanted it, so
they agreed to leave it in the middle.

13
00:00:47,920 --> 00:00:51,690
Bangkok's full ceremonial
name has 168 letters,

14
00:00:51,730 --> 00:00:55,095
so locals just call it the City of Angels.

15
00:00:55,635 --> 00:00:58,140
Thailand is home to the bumblebee bat,

16
00:00:58,180 --> 00:01:01,824
the smallest bat on Earth,
about as big as a bumblebee.

17
00:01:02,767 --> 00:01:04,734
Now, a few surprising places.

18
00:01:06,550 --> 00:01:10,008
In Chiang Rai, the White
Temple looks like frozen snow,

19
00:01:10,048 --> 00:01:13,633
and it was built by one artist
who is still adding to it.

20
00:01:14,173 --> 00:01:17,716
In Samut Songkhram, a train
rolls right through a market,

21
00:01:17,756 --> 00:01:21,048
and the vendors pull back
their awnings just in time.

22
00:01:21,588 --> 00:01:25,130
In Lopburi, thousands of monkeys
take over the old town,

23
00:01:25,170 --> 00:01:27,688
and every year they get their own feast.

24
00:01:28,228 --> 00:01:31,778
In Ayutthaya, a stone Buddha
head sits inside the roots

25
00:01:31,818 --> 00:01:34,780
of a tree, and the tree
slowly grew around it.

26
00:01:35,733 --> 00:01:37,131
Let's talk about culture.

27
00:01:38,950 --> 00:01:43,071
The national dish is pad thai,
noodles stir fried with egg

28
00:01:43,111 --> 00:01:46,729
and peanuts, pushed
by the government in the 1940s.

29
00:01:47,269 --> 00:01:50,859
The traditional outfit
is the chut thai, a wrapped silk

30
00:01:50,899 --> 00:01:54,686
skirt and a fitted top, worn
at weddings and royal events.

31
00:01:55,226 --> 00:01:58,499
And the classic instrument
is the ranat ek, a wooden

32
00:01:58,539 --> 00:02:01,875
xylophone, the lead voice
of the old court orchestra.

33
00:02:02,800 --> 00:02:04,142
Time for a little history.

34
00:02:05,950 --> 00:02:08,500
In 1238, the kingdom of Sukhothai rose,

35
00:02:08,540 --> 00:02:11,779
and Thais still call it their first kingdom.

36
00:02:12,319 --> 00:02:15,847
In 1782, King Rama the First
founded Bangkok

37
00:02:15,887 --> 00:02:19,090
and the dynasty that still reigns today.

38
00:02:19,630 --> 00:02:23,075
In 1896, Britain and France
agreed to keep Siam

39
00:02:23,115 --> 00:02:26,338
as a buffer, and that is how
it stayed free.

40
00:02:26,878 --> 00:02:30,482
In 1932, a bloodless
revolution ended absolute

41
00:02:30,522 --> 00:02:34,285
rule and made the king
a constitutional monarch.

42
00:02:35,233 --> 00:02:37,172
So, what does $10 get you here?

43
00:02:38,950 --> 00:02:43,277
A plate of pad thai from a street
cart costs about $1.50.

44
00:02:43,817 --> 00:02:46,065
An iced Thai tea costs about $1.

45
00:02:46,605 --> 00:02:50,375
A mango sticky rice
dessert costs about $2.40.

46
00:02:50,915 --> 00:02:55,207
A can of Chang beer
at 7-Eleven costs about $1.60.

47
00:02:55,747 --> 00:02:59,137
A short Bangkok sky train
ride costs about $1.

48
00:02:59,677 --> 00:03:02,623
So with $10, you get
a street meal, a dessert,

49
00:03:02,663 --> 00:03:05,090
a beer, a ride, and still have change.

50
00:03:06,033 --> 00:03:08,074
Before you go, here's the don't list.

51
00:03:09,817 --> 00:03:13,105
Don't point your feet
at a person or a Buddha statue.

52
00:03:13,145 --> 00:03:16,307
Feet are the lowest part
of the body, so it's rude.

53
00:03:16,847 --> 00:03:17,930
Don't bring a vape.

54
00:03:17,970 --> 00:03:21,123
Tourists have been fined
or arrested for carrying one.

55
00:03:21,663 --> 00:03:26,053
Don't climb on a Buddha statue
or pose disrespectfully for a photo.

56
00:03:26,093 --> 00:03:28,169
Tourists have been fined for it.

57
00:03:28,709 --> 00:03:30,601
Don't ever insult the monarchy.

58
00:03:30,641 --> 00:03:33,468
It's illegal, and it can
mean years in prison.

59
00:03:34,400 --> 00:03:38,464
And now, the chapter you were all
waiting for: legends and mysteries.

60
00:03:40,283 --> 00:03:44,978
Mae Nak was a young wife in old
Bangkok, near the Phra Khanong canal.

61
00:03:45,018 --> 00:03:48,890
She died in childbirth while
her husband was away at war.

62
00:03:48,930 --> 00:03:53,968
The story says her ghost kept living
with him, looking like a woman again.

63
00:03:54,008 --> 00:03:56,301
A monk finally trapped her spirit.

64
00:03:56,341 --> 00:04:01,105
Today her shrine at Wat Mahabut
is one of the most visited in Bangkok.

65
00:04:01,645 --> 00:04:03,966
Then there are the Naga fireballs.

66
00:04:04,006 --> 00:04:07,090
Every October, near
the end of Buddhist Lent,

67
00:04:07,130 --> 00:04:10,631
red lights rise from the Mekong
River in Nong Khai.

68
00:04:10,671 --> 00:04:14,311
Thousands of people gather
on the riverbank to watch.

69
00:04:14,351 --> 00:04:18,199
Locals say a giant serpent,
the Naga, is breathing fire.

70
00:04:18,239 --> 00:04:22,157
Scientists suggest glowing
gas, but nobody has proven it.

71
00:04:22,697 --> 00:04:27,706
Now the mystery of Jim Thompson,
the American who revived Thai silk.

72
00:04:27,746 --> 00:04:33,276
On Easter Sunday, 1967, he went for a walk
in Malaysia's Cameron Highlands.

73
00:04:33,316 --> 00:04:34,687
He never came back.

74
00:04:34,727 --> 00:04:37,360
A huge search found no trace of him.

75
00:04:37,400 --> 00:04:40,330
To this day, nobody knows what happened.

76
00:04:43,566 --> 00:04:44,578
That was Thailand.

77
00:04:44,618 --> 00:04:46,623
Which country should we visit next?

78
00:04:46,663 --> 00:04:48,025
Tell me in the comments.
